<p><a href="/en/cases/nivellux.html">NIVELLUX</a> needed a clear presentation of its services and experience. This example shows how a small website can be assessed through its content and enquiry journey.</p>
<p><a href="/en/cases/shepit-house.html">SHEPIT HOUSE</a> required additional tools to help buyers choose. The $1000 figure covers website development. Advertising and other work described in the wider case study are not included in that amount.</p>
<p><a href="/en/cases/delmar-custom-crm.html">Estate CRM for DELMAR</a> addresses internal agency processes. It connects enquiries, properties, selections and team oversight, illustrating how broad web development can be.</p>
<p>The cost of a similar new project depends on functionality, content readiness, languages, data sources and integration requirements. A company website with a CMS and administration panel also needs a defined scope first. A CRM price cannot automatically be applied to any corporate website.</p>
<h2>How we choose the format and prepare an estimate</h2>
<p>We start with the business: what it sells, to whom, where enquiries will come from and what should happen afterwards.</p>
<p>Then we describe user journeys. Should visitors simply request a selection, or compare properties themselves? Are separate advertising pages needed? Who updates the data? Which business areas will grow through search?</p>
<p>We then develop the structure and identify the necessary modules. The estimate distinguishes pages, content work, catalogue management, forms, analytics, language versions and integrations. The client can see what affects the cost and what could move to a later phase.</p>
<p>A landing page can be expanded into a larger website. If that is already the plan, the technology and content organisation should support it. A complete rebuild should not come as a surprise after the first campaign.</p>
<p>We discuss the budget in more detail in our article on <a href="/en/materials/development/stoimost-razrabotki-v-eru-ai/">website development costs in the AI era</a>.</p>
<h2>What to prepare before choosing a format</h2>
<p>For an initial discussion, describe the offer, audience, advertising and SEO plans, number of properties or services, and enquiry handling process. Existing websites, materials and examples of what works or causes problems are also useful.</p>
<p>For testing a specific offer, we can consider a landing page. For a catalogue, several business areas and search growth, we can design a broader website structure. In both cases, the scope and cost are agreed before development begins.</p>
